  "mechanismSummary": "The terminal oxygen of cumene hydroperoxide is protonated, and as water leaves the phenyl group moves from carbon to the inner oxygen: an oxocarbenium ion. Water adds, and proton transfers let phenol leave from the hemiketal, giving acetone. This is the last stage of the cumene process, which makes most of the world's phenol and acetone from benzene, propene and air.",
